# LV2 syscalls the ELF makes, one number per line (PS3 Health's tools/syscalls.py
# --allow checks the ELF against this file; --write rewrites it from a
# known-good ELF and drops these notes). Written on 2026-10-11 from Couch
# 0.1.0's second ELF (the first had one sc the scanner could not resolve: gcc
# put sysUsleep's li r11 after the sc, so it went through nap(), until the
# exit's fix below removed that loop), each
# number looked at before it went in: 39 numbers, 79
# call sites, every sc resolved. They are PS3 Health's runtime set without its
# drive, temperature and fan calls (383, 409, 600, 601, 609, 616): threads and
# time (44, 141, 142, 145, 146), memory (330, 331, 337), the tty (402, 403),
# the network (700 to 714) and the file system (801 to 834), from PSL1GHT's
# runtime and ps3gfx. Couch's own calls add no number: libnet, libnetctl,
# sysModuleLoad and sysUtilGetSystemParamInt are SPRX imports, and
# sysLv2FsStat (808) and sysUsleep (141) were in the set already. The exit's
# fix of 2026-10-11 (board_stop shuts the socket down and joins with no wait
# loop, so nap() went; net_end) keeps these 39 numbers at 78 call sites,
# every sc resolved: netShutdown, netCtlTerm, netDeinitialize and
# sysModuleUnload add no number. On 2026-10-13 (Couch 0.3.0, stage 8 of
# the revamp design: the effects' SPU group, source/spu_fx_run.c) the nine
# SPU numbers of PS3 Health and Cell Bench came in, each looked at in the
# audit's list: 165 (a thread's exit status), 169 (sysSpuInitialize), 170
# (the group's create), 171 (its destroy), 172 (a thread's initialize), 173
# (the group's start), 177 (its terminate), 178 (its join) and 190 (a
# mailbox word): 48 numbers at 93 call sites, every sc resolved. The
# image's import and close are SPRX imports (no number). On 2026-10-16
# (Couch 0.5.0: the Info page's Hardware row, info.c) two of PS3 Health's
# read-only calls came in, made as Health makes them and journaled under
# Health's names: 383 (sys_game_get_temperature: the Cell and the RSX,
# "temps") and 409 (sys_sm_get_fan_policy: the fan duty, "fan_policy",
# behind its first-run prompt as in Health). Never 602, 604 or 870: the
# script refuses them whatever this file says.
